      <tei:div type="colophon" subtype="notes">
        <tei:p>The hymn “Although the vine its fruit deny” by Abraham Moïse (ca.1799-1869), is presented as Hymn 1 in <tei:hi rend="italic">The Sabbath service and miscellaneous prayers, adopted by the Reformed society of Israelites, founded in Charleston, S.C., November 21, 1825</tei:hi> (1830), p. 55. The attribution to Abraham Moïse is based on handwritten annotation found in a copy of the prayerbook, a photostat copy of which is in the American Jewish Archives. –Aharon Varady</tei:p>
      </tei:div>
